  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "💆 Massage Business Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Professional names for a massage therapist, clinic or mobile massage business."
    },
    "intro": "Good massage business names sound calm and professional, say what kind of massage you offer, and can't be misread. The **Massage Business Name Generator** suggests names for a massage therapy practice, sports massage clinic or mobile massage therapist: catchy, classic and professional, modern, sports and remedial, holistic, your town or your own name.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good massage business names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Dunmore Remedial Massage</strong>: a surname and \"remedial\" sounds clinical and trusted.</li><li><strong>Castle Street Massage Therapists</strong>: a street name and a clear job title.</li><li><strong>Grounded Sports Massage</strong>: modern, and says who it's for.</li><li><strong>Comeback Sports Massage</strong>: speaks straight to injured athletes.</li><li><strong>Full Range Performance Massage</strong>: a sports name that sounds like results.</li><li><strong>Still Point Holistic Therapies</strong>: a calm holistic name.</li><li><strong>Aches Away Massage</strong>: a gentle, catchy promise.</li><li><strong>Unknotted Massage Therapy</strong>: a light pun that stays professional.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How massage business names work",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Say the kind of massage.</strong> Clients search for sports, deep tissue, remedial or pregnancy massage, so put the one you specialise in into the name: <em>Comeback Sports Massage</em>.</li><li><strong>Clinical words build trust.</strong> Therapy, therapist, clinic and practice tell people this is a professional treatment: <em>Corbett Massage Clinic</em>.</li><li><strong>Holistic names</strong> suit reflexology, reiki and relaxation massage: <em>Fieldstone Massage & Reiki</em>.</li><li><strong>Keep puns gentle.</strong> Anything that could be read as a different kind of business will put off the clients you want.</li></ul><p>Rules on titles differ by country. In the US, many states license massage therapists and control who can advertise massage or use the title \"massage therapist\", and some ask for a licence number in adverts. Check your state board before you choose a name.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
        "content": "<p>Press <strong>Check</strong> on any name, or paste one into the <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a>, to see whether the domain and social handles are free and to jump to the company register and trade mark searches. Then:</p><ul><li><strong>Search the company register.</strong> In the UK that's Companies House; in the US, your state's business register.</li><li><strong>Search trade marks</strong> with the UK Intellectual Property Office or the USPTO, especially if you'll sell products or open more than one site.</li><li><strong>Look locally.</strong> Search Google Maps for massage therapists near you: a similar name a few streets away will confuse customers even if it's legally fine.</li></ul><p>This is general guidance, not legal advice. For more on choosing and checking a name, read our guide: <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Mobile and home-based therapists",
